extraction_notes: "THE TWO CHASSIS ARE `variants` OVERRIDING `mdc_base` ONLY (130 and 200 main body), and everything else about them is in the abilities. Their fixed P.S., P.P. and Speed are NOT stored: these are an O.C.C., whose attribute block is minimums rather than rolls, and the full-conversion figures replace a character''s attributes rather than setting a floor - and the Full Construction chassis prints P.S. as a RANGE, 28-30, which is neither a fixed value nor dice. Free Quebec''s five cyborg classes set the same precedent on printed 114-116: the chassis body, its M.D.C. by location, its armour schedule and its weapon systems are a `vehicles` row imported from the same pages, and the class carries only `mdc_base` and a pointer. THE NEW WEST VESSEL IMPORT HAS NOT RUN YET - printed 171-223 is a later batch - so there is no vessel row to point at, and the full M.D.C.-by-location figures are in the ability text until there is. `mdc_base` holds the MAIN BODY only; the bionic body armour on top of it (120 and 150) is part of the chassis rather than of the character. Standard Equipment stores only the catalog rows that exist; the book also lists light to medium M.D.C. body armour, a quality cowboy hat, a poncho or cloak, tinted goggles, a large wooden cross, a cigarette lighter, a magnifying glass, a pocket mirror, 150 feet of heavy cord or cable, a pick axe, a shovel, a sledgehammer, a mallet, a tool kit, four small sacks and 1D4 large ones, a survival knife and two weapons of choice with three spare clips each, one type-one fusion block, 48 blasting cartridges at 2D6 M.D. apiece, and 36 flares. The book also prints WAGES rather than only a purse: 100 credits a week while working off the augmentation, or 400-1000 a week freelance, both with room and board; `starting_money` holds the figure the book gives for one who has turned to adventuring."
